---
/*
 * The one thing this page cannot give you yet, said once, under the three things it can.
 *
 * WHAT IS TRUE, AND WHERE IT WAS CHECKED. Every line number below was RE-READ on this pass
 * against supabase/functions/command/index.ts, not carried over — and every one of them had
 * drifted from the figures the retired /start components cited, which is the argument for
 * re-reading them. The dead numbers are named so a future reader can tell drift from a
 * different claim: the gate was cited at :2182 and is at :2250; the credential and
 * verification gates at :2183-2186 are at :2251-2254; the live-workspace count at :2245-2251
 * is at :2320-2325; identityVerified at :3205 is at :3477.
 *
 *   the handler EXISTS ..... `create_workspace` is served by createSelfServeWorkspace()
 *                            (:2231), dispatched at :2780 ahead of route resolution because a
 *                            brand-new caller has no membership to resolve against.
 *   and it is GATED ........ `const selfServeEnabled = Deno.env.get("SWARM_SELF_SERVE") ===
 *                            "1"` (:323), and the handler's FIRST line is
 *                            `if (!selfServeEnabled) return await forbid(...)` (:2250) —
 *                            a 403, before anything else is looked at. Production does not
 *                            set the variable.
 *   3 live workspaces ...... FREE_TIER_WORKSPACE_LIMIT = 3 (:330), compared against a count
 *                            with `AND archived_at IS NULL` (:2323) — archiving one frees the
 *                            slot, which is why this says "live" and not just "three".
 *   verified identity ...... a non-human credential is refused (:2251), then an unverified
 *                            one (:2254); identityVerified is email_confirmed_at (:3477).
 *   no card ................ no billing surface exists in this repo. Re-enumerated with a
 *                            control on this pass: stripe|billing|payment|subscription|
 *                            invoice|\bprice\b over src/, supabase/functions/,
 *                            supabase/migrations/ and package.json is 0 matching lines,
 *                            against 684 for "workspace" over the same paths — so the grep
 *                            runs and the zero is a zero. (The earlier note recorded 1002 for
 *                            the control; the difference is that count and this one were
 *                            taken with different flags, not that the tree shrank. What both
 *                            establish is the same thing: the instrument fires.)
 *
 * TWO SENTENCES THAT MUST NOT BE COLLAPSED INTO ONE. "There is no self-serve signup" is DEAD
 * and false — the handler is there. "Signup is open" is also false — the gate is off. The
 * panel says built AND not switched on, in that order, because that pair survives launch day:
 * when SWARM_SELF_SERVE flips, only the second half is edited.
 *
 * WHY THE LINK GOES TO THE PRICING CARD AND IS NOT LABELLED "ASK FOR AN INVITE". The home
 * page's #invite section carries an email field whose own hint reads "Nothing is sent. There
 * is no service behind this button yet." Sending someone there under a call to action that
 * implies a request reaches somebody would be this site's worst habit, committed by a link
 * label. The link names what is actually at the other end: the terms of the free tier.
 *
 * NO STUB CONTROL ON THIS PAGE. The wizard this panel replaced had a GitHub button that
 * existed to fail and a form that created nothing. A disabled button captioned "coming soon"
 * would be the same idea with worse manners; a sentence is enough.
 */
---

<aside class="own" aria-labelledby="own-t">
  <h2 class="own__t" id="own-t">No invite yet?</h2>
  <p class="own__p">
    Today the way in is an invitation from someone already in a workspace — that is the link
    step two accepts. Starting your own is built and isn’t switched on here yet, so there’s
    nothing on this page that would do it.
  </p>
  <p class="own__p">
    When it opens: three live workspaces per verified identity, free, and no card at any
    point. <a href="/#invite">What the free tier includes</a>.
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .own {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-10);
    padding: var(--pad-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--bg-raised);
  }

  /* Deliberately a step DOWN from the step headings above it: this is the aside, and the
     three commands are the page. Same reason it has no button. */
  .own__t {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--t-base);
    line-height: var(--lh-base);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-head);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .own__p {
    margin: var(--s-2) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-sm);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .own__p a {
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--border-strong);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    transition: text-decoration-color var(--dur-2) var(--ease-standard);
  }

  .own__p a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }
</style>
